                    "line": 9,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Originally we were going to allow different association names.  For instance you see \"inventory\" and \"sensors\", but you could also have \"inventory\" and \"controllers\" (just making up one) and so in that case you'd have multiple reverse-names for inventory.  As we've refined what associations look like, this should now no longer be the case."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Oliver Brewka",
                        "email": "oliver.brewka@9elements.com",
                        "username": "mox669"
                    },
                    "message": "Considering, that some of the association definitions were already written as a list and using the correct spelling of `reverse_name:`, this unifies the definitions to the correct style. LGTM"
                }
            ],
